# Style guides

Use the style guides to check a word, a punctuation mark or a number. They settle questions the [writing guidelines](../writing-guidelines/index.html) do not.

| Style guide | Use it for |
| --- | --- |
| [A to Z style guide](a-to-z.html) | Capital letters, punctuation, numbers, dates, times and common words |
| [Technical A to Z](technical-a-to-z.html) | Home Assistant terms: entities, states, attributes, automations and the interface |

## How to use them

1. Look up the word in the Technical A to Z first. If it is not there, look in the A to Z.
2. If a word is in neither, use the rule in [Use clear language](../writing-guidelines/clear-language.html).
3. If a rule needs to change, record it as an [exception](../publish-update-retire/update.html) and say why.

Both guides keep native Home Assistant labels as they are. A rule about wording never changes a translation, a screen label or a name someone gave a device.
